4. CARE, MAINTENANCE, AND STANDARDS
4.1 Lessee shall provide proper care and exercise good judgment in maintaining the Horse in good health and condition.
4.2 Lessee shall follow accepted standards of good husbandry, including but not limited to:
•	Regular veterinary attention
•	Required vaccinations
•	Adequate feed and water
•	Proper shelter and supervision
4.3 The Horse shall be maintained in condition comparable to its condition at the commencement of this Agreement, reasonable wear excepted.

5. EXPENSES
5.1 Lessee shall be solely responsible for all costs during the lease term, including but not limited to:
•	Boarding
•	Farrier services
•	Transportation
•	Show and competition expenses
5.2 Lessor shall remain responsible for regular veterinary care, except as otherwise provided herein.
5.3 All expenses incurred by Lessee shall be personal obligations of Lessee and shall not create any lien or claim against the Horse.

6. STABLING LOCATION
The Horse’s principal stable shall be located at:

Temporary relocation is permitted for shows or events, provided prior approval is obtained from Lessor for any permanent change in stabling location.

7. LIABILITY AND RELEASE
The Lessee assumes all risk associated with the Horse during the term of this Agreement.
The Lessor shall not be liable for any loss, injury, damage, claim, or expense arising from the Horse’s use, handling, or stabling, whether involving persons or animals.
Lessee hereby releases and holds harmless the Lessor from all related claims, including legal costs.

8. INSURANCE AND LOSS
8.1 The Horse is valued at $-------- and shall be insured by Lessee against death and theft for such amount.
8.2 Lessee shall maintain the insurance policy in full force and bear all premiums.
8.3 In the event of theft, death, or euthanasia while under Lessee’s care, insurance proceeds shall constitute full compensation to Lessor, provided proper veterinary care was administered and Lessor was promptly notified.

9. PRE-EXISTING CONDITIONS
Lessor shall not hold Lessee responsible for death or extraordinary veterinary treatment resulting from any medical conditions existing at the commencement of this Agreement.

10. OWNERSHIP
The Horse shall remain the sole and exclusive property of the Lessor.
Nothing in this Agreement shall transfer any ownership interest to Lessee except as expressly provided herein.

11. RIGHT OF FIRST REFUSAL
If during the lease term the Horse is offered for sale and a bona fide third-party offer is received, Lessee shall have the right to match such offer and purchase the Horse before acceptance of any other offer.

12. DEFAULT AND TERMINATION
Failure by Lessee to make payments or properly care for the Horse shall constitute default, entitling Lessor to immediate termination and repossession of the Horse.

